KG42.register("rules-09cfc628fc112e6211f11361",{"id":"34-market_versus_price_scheduling::v141-c-R012","paper":"34-market_versus_price_scheduling","record":{"rule_id":"v141-c-R012","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M02","name":"Price-signal coordination","process_stage":"coordination","market_meaning":"The microgrid controller determines the least-cost schedule of available DERs, loads and main-grid power transfer using day-ahead market prices forecast by the microgrid or electric utility. Scope: Price-based microgrid optimal scheduling benchmark, using forecast day-ahead market prices.","independence_rationale":"Relations governed by the approved function coordination.price_signal under the fixed relation-ownership template. Conditional branches retain their explicit scope in local constraints.","V":["coordination.price_signal"],"E":[],"omega":{"market_type":"DEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"coordination","context_text":"Price-based microgrid optimal scheduling benchmark, using forecast day-ahead market prices.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e005"]},"x":[],"theta":[],"phi":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R012-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The microgrid controller determines the least-cost schedule of available DERs, loads and main-grid power transfer using day-ahead market prices forecast by the microgrid or electric utility. Scope: Price-based microgrid optimal scheduling benchmark, using forecast day-ahead market prices.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.price_signal"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e005"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R012-C002","kind":"procedural","role":"supporting","statement":"In the price-based scheduling method, the ISO receives load forecasts from Electric Distribution Companies, solves a security-constrained unit commitment (SCUC) problem to determine day-ahead unit schedules, and determines locational marginal prices (LMPs) that microgrids use for scheduling.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.price_signal"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e028"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R012-C003","kind":"procedural","role":"supporting","statement":"In the price-based method, main-grid power transfer is determined via a local cost-minimization problem rather than by the DMO via a market mechanism.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.price_signal"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e030"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R012-C004","kind":"procedural","role":"supporting","statement":"In Case 1 (price-based scheduling), the ISO uses forecasted microgrid loads to clear the market and determine hourly LMP values; microgrids individually perform their own scheduling using those LMP values.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.price_signal"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E24"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R012-C005","kind":"procedural","role":"supporting","statement":"Under the price-based scheme, the utility forecasts an estimate of microgrid loads in its service territory and submits it to the system operator; once the wholesale-market electricity price is determined, the utility sends the actual prices to microgrids.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.price_signal"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e006"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R012-C006","kind":"procedural","role":"supporting","statement":"In the price-based model, the actual amount of load at the microgrid bus may differ from the amount originally considered by the ISO when clearing the wholesale market; re-running economic dispatch with actual microgrid net loads would change LMPs, creating a mutual and uncontrolled interaction between calculated LMPs and microgrid net load.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.price_signal"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E25"]}],"pi":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e005","location":{"location_id":"src-b66ae5184e-p02-c1r3__v141-a-M02-participation","page":2,"printed_page":null,"section":"I. Introduction","anchor_text":"p p Increasing demand-side elasticity and active participation of as loads in the power system, comm","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-02.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"However, these resources are typically scheduled based on a price-based scheduling model, i.e., the microgrid controller determines the least-cost schedule of available DERs and loads, as well as the main grid power transfer, based on the day-ahead market prices (which are forecasted by the microgrid or the electric utility)."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e006","location":{"location_id":"src-b66ae5184e-p02-c1r4__v141-a-M02-coordination","page":2,"printed_page":null,"section":"I. Introduction","anchor_text":"ator. Once the price of electricity is determined, through the po wholesale market, the utility send","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-02.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"Under this scheme, the utility forecasts an estimate of the microgrids’ loads in its service territory and submits to the system operator. Once the price of electricity is determined, through the wholesale market, the utility sends the actual prices to microgrids."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e028","location":{"location_id":"src-b66ae5184e-p04-c2r2__v141-a-M02-clearing","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":"III. Model Outline","anchor_text":"investigated in numerical simulations. In the price-based scheduling method, the ISO receives load f","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"In the price-based scheduling method, the ISO receives load forecasts from Electric Distribution Companies (EDC) and determines the day-ahead unit schedules by solving a security-constrained unit commitment (SCUC) problem. The ISO will also determine locational marginal prices (LMPs) which will be further used by microgrids for scheduling purposes."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e030","location":{"location_id":"src-b66ae5184e-p04-c2r2__v141-a-M02-clearing","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":"III. Model Outline","anchor_text":"investigated in numerical simulations. In the price-based scheduling method, the ISO receives load f","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"...and moreover, the main grid power transfer will be determined via a local cost minimization problem rather than being determined by the DMO via a market mechanism."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E24","location":{"location_id":"src-b66ae5184e-p06-c2r4__v141-a-M02-clearing","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":"V. Numerical Simulations / Case 1","anchor_text":"grid loads to clear the market and accordingly determine hourly LMP values. Microgrids individually ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"example"},"source_text":"Case 1: In this case, the ISO uses the forecasted microgrid loads to clear the market and accordingly determine hourly LMP values. Microgrids individually perform their own scheduling using the LMP values."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E25","location":{"location_id":"src-b66ae5184e-p06-c2r4__v141-a-M02-coordination","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":"V. Numerical Simulations / Case 1","anchor_text":"grid loads to clear the market and accordingly determine hourly LMP values. Microgrids individually ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"In this case, the actual amount of load at the bus to which microgrids are connected will not match the amount originally considered by the ISO when clearing the wholesale market. If the ISO runs the economic dispatch with the actual microgrids net loads, which would be less than the microgrid load used initially by the ISO to determine the LMPs, the prices would change. This change in LMPs can be considered as a major drawback in the price-based model where there is a mutual and uncontrolled interaction between the calculated LMPs and microgrids net load. Another drawback that needs to be considered is that the mismatch between the initially forecasted load and the actual load, after microgrid optimal scheduling, needs to be addressed by the ISO by redispatching the committed units. The redispatch will potentially result in an economic loss for the system as the new solution will diverge from the already determined optimal dispatch solution."}],"field_notes":{"empty_E_reason":"C explicitly supplied only source-backed unary facts for this function; other graph gaps remain reviewable.","empty_x_reason":"No variable symbol, domain, or unit is defined in this rule's same-mechanism evidence or frozen graph; C.1 explicitly left x empty as a graph-draft limitation, not a source conclusion. The described DER outputs, load, and main-grid transfer lack typed objects here.","empty_theta_reason":"Day-ahead prices and LMPs are described in prose, but the rule evidence supplies no symbol, domain, value, or unit and the graph has no parameter objects; C.1 left theta empty."},"evidence_basis":"explicit","implementation_status":"unimplemented","status":"needs_review","lead_ids":["v141-a-M02-clearing","v141-a-M02-coordination","v141-a-M02-pricing"],"extras":{"decision_anchor":"coordination.price_signal","graph_fact_supports":[[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e005","quote":"the microgrid controller determines the least-cost schedule of available DERs and loads, as well as the main grid power transfer, based on the day-ahead market prices (which are forecasted by the microgrid or the electric utility)."}]],"C2_formalization":{"graph_sha256":"54c0ba07ab404a684efa8bfd07efbeb6e0d82179dae983e9c36af720e5737c0c","applicability":"needs_revision","reason":"Preserved C.1's procedural price-signal coordination statement. The same-mechanism candidate texts describe ISO SCUC/LMP formation, utility price delivery, local cost minimization for main-grid transfer, and the LMP/net-load interaction, but they provide no explicit optimization formula or symbol definitions for this rule. The frozen graph has only coordination.price_signal with E empty and no x/theta, so the least-cost scheduling relation cannot be expressed without C.1 adding typed objects and relationships. Evidence is unreviewed under this experiment; no source audit is claimed.","bindings":[{"object_id":"v141-c-R012-C001","node_ids":["coordination.price_signal"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"C.1 core procedural statement is attached to the only frozen coordination node; no edges exist in the frozen graph."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R012-C002","node_ids":["coordination.price_signal"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"C002 records the ISO LMP-setting process as supporting the price signal; attached to coordination.price_signal, with no frozen edge present."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R012-C003","node_ids":["coordination.price_signal"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"C003 records local cost minimization of main-grid transfer as part of price-based coordination; attached to coordination.price_signal, with no frozen edge present."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R012-C004","node_ids":["coordination.price_signal"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"C004 records Case 1 price-based clearing and microgrid scheduling from LMPs; attached to coordination.price_signal, with no frozen edge present."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R012-C005","node_ids":["coordination.price_signal"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"C005 records utility forecasting and delivery of actual wholesale prices to microgrids; attached to coordination.price_signal, with no frozen edge present."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R012-C006","node_ids":["coordination.price_signal"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"C006 records the LMP/net-load interaction drawback in price-based coordination; attached to coordination.price_signal, with no frozen edge present."}],"revision_requests":["C.1: Add typed variable objects for the microgrid scheduling decision quantities (for example, DER output, load/demand, and main-grid power transfer) only where source definitions, indices, domains, units, and same-mechanism evidence are available; otherwise explicitly confirm that this rule remains procedural.","C.1: Add a typed parameter for the day-ahead price/LMP signal if source definitions provide its symbol, indices, unit, and rule-scoped meaning; do not infer it from general nomenclature without same-rule support.","C.1: Add the graph edges needed to represent the price signal entering the microgrid least-cost scheduling relation, or explicitly state that the graph intentionally represents only a unary coordination fact.","B/C.1: Re-extract and verify the explicit price-based local cost-minimization objective and constraints; current evidence states only that such a local cost-minimization problem determines main-grid transfer.","B/C.1: Reconcile the price-setter scope across candidate evidence (utility forecast/price delivery, ISO SCUC/LMP formation, and DMO-determined price); this ambiguity is unresolved and was not formalized."]}},"quarantined_references":[]}});
